GFC Friend Pack — turn your game clips into frames for {collector_name}'s school ML project

1. Right-click this zip > Extract All. Open the extracted folder.
2. Drag a folder of clips (ONE game per folder) onto "START HERE.bat".
   Or double-click it and drag the folder into the window.
3. The first time, type your name and answer two yes/no questions.
4. Pick the game, press Enter a few times, and wait. You can close the
   window any time; run it again on the same folder to continue.
5. Send the zip it makes (in the "output" folder) as a Google Drive,
   OneDrive or WeTransfer link. Discord's free limit is too small.

What it does: samples one picture every 5 seconds from each clip, plus a
low-quality copy of the same picture, and saves basic video info (file
names, recording dates, resolution, length). No audio, no video, nothing uploaded. Your
clips are only read, never changed. Everything stays on {collector_name}'s
PC for this project. Ask and it gets deleted.

If Windows says "Windows protected your PC": click More info > Run anyway.
(Or before extracting: right-click the zip > Properties > tick Unblock.)

Steam recordings: export the clip to MP4 in Steam first.
It uses a lot of CPU while running; that's normal.
Problems? Send {collector_contact} the file output\...\run_log.txt.
